  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth4Governance: Empowering Lebanese Youth to Catalyze Public Sector Reform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon is facing severe crises, including one of the worst economic collapses in history, with a GDP contraction of nearly 30% since 2020 and inflation exceeding 250% by mid-2023. Political mismanagement has created a polarized environment, undermining democratic institutions and disproportionately affecting youth, whose unemployment reached 47.8% in 2022. A significant number of young people (77%) express a desire to emigrate, contributing to a brain drain of nearly 900k citizens between 2019 and 2022.
Public dissatisfaction with services is widespread, with a dysfunctional Gov-to-Citizen relationship. The Youth4Governance program, launched by Siren and Saint Joseph University in 2021, aims to engage youth in public sector reform. The program has trained 100 interns in technology and public policy to improve gov efficiency and accountability. Expanding to multiple universities, Y4G promotes a sustainable model of youth involvement in governance, fostering positive change in Lebanon.</narrative>
  </description>
